<title>GERMANY: Germany hopes Britain in EMU in 1999.</title>
<headline>Germany hopes Britain in EMU in 1999.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Foreign Minister Klaus Kinkel on Friday repeated the government's insistence that European economic and monetary union (EMU) will take place on time in 1999 and said he hoped Britain would be a founding member.</p>
<p>&quot;Monetary union must not and should not be delayed,&quot; Kinkel said in an interview with the Koelner Express newspaper.</p>
<p>Asked about Britain's doubts that EMU would start on time, Kinkel said that in the financial community some 60 percent of those polled now expected EMU to take place on time.</p>
<p>&quot;We would like Great Britain to be there,&quot; Kinkel said.</p>
<p>The participants in the first wave of EMU in 1999 will be chosen next year based on their financial performance in 1997. EMU participants must keep a tight hold on public debt and budget deficits.</p>
<p>-- William Boston, Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
